  "narrative": "No assessments were due, and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. I therefore treated all released validation intervals already present in the ledger as confirmatory evidence and made no new validation request. All estimates below are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 claims, positive signed support means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is more negative, i.e. stronger dependency_composite. For direction +1 claims, positive signed support means the raw contrast is less negative or more positive, i.e. weaker dependency_composite. The absolute threshold for a scientifically meaningful dependency-composite difference remains 0.15 units. I downgraded H127 and H134 from accepted to unresolved and closed them because their interval lower bounds fall below the effect-size threshold or the null, despite point estimates above threshold; this is a stricter threshold-robustness judgment for smaller context-specific PTEN claims. I also closed redundant middle Cas9, screen-quality, growth-rate, and middle aneuploidy PTEN claims to leave a smaller active set for the remaining high-value tests. Supported within-dataset associations are concentrated in four large predictor contrasts and one smaller predictor contrast. SMARCA4 loss is robustly associated with stronger dependency: signed discovery +0.833 with lower +0.767 (R4) and independent validation +0.803 with lower +0.710 (R13). This association survives in many biological and technical strata, including MSI-negative cells signed +0.840 lower +0.774 (R195) and the middle mutation-burden band signed +0.839 lower +0.748 (R198). KEAP1 loss is robustly associated with weaker dependency: signed discovery +0.832 lower +0.766 (R6, direction reversed to H13) and validation +0.795 lower +0.702 (R26), with replication in MSI-negative cells +0.844 lower +0.781 (R196) and the middle mutation-burden band +0.812 lower +0.718 (R199). TP53 loss is robustly associated with weaker dependency: signed discovery +0.423 lower +0.327 (R1) and validation +0.384 lower +0.239 (R39), with replication in MSI-negative cells +0.425 lower +0.328 (R197) and the middle mutation-burden band +0.408 lower +0.268 (R200). MSI-high is robustly associated with stronger dependency: signed discovery +0.792 lower +0.676 (R88/H101) and validation +0.815 lower +0.651 (R93), and it remains strong in the middle mutation-burden band +0.849 lower +0.693 (R189). PTEN loss is a smaller but recurrent stronger-dependency association: overall signed +0.227 lower +0.131 (R9) with validation +0.338 lower +0.198 (R66), and it is supported in selected cleaner or threshold-relevant contexts, including TP53-intact cells +0.259 lower +0.169 (R132), triple-intact TP53/SMARCA4/KEAP1 cells +0.252 lower +0.169 with validation direction replication but lower validation bound below threshold +0.186 lower +0.066 (R44/R53), triple-intact MSI-negative cells +0.260 lower +0.182 (R205), and triple-intact low-aneuploidy cells +0.297 lower +0.156 (R203). Negative or unsupported findings are substantial. KRAS mutation, MTAP loss, ARID1A loss, STK11 loss, CDKN2A loss, BRCA2 loss, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, APC mutation, SMAD4 loss, NF1 loss, BRAF V600E, MYC amplification overall and under high MYC expression, and the constructed binary markers D, E, and F did not show threshold-relevant effects. Media serum, screen batch, CRISPR library categories, matched RNA/DNA availability, RNA omics availability, and sex did not provide stable supported effects; sex initially had a small discovery signal but failed validation signed -0.013 with lower -0.104 (R80). Interaction analyses were generally null, below threshold, or failed validation; the adenocarcinoma KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction that had discovery support did not survive validation signed -0.134 with lower -0.563 (R107). Therefore I do not claim a supported interaction effect. Unresolved uncertainty remains mainly in context-specific PTEN behavior and direct continuous research-signature associations. The direct signature attempts with exposure set to continuous values returned insufficient-cell implementation failures rather than null evidence, so signature effects remain untested in a valid form. MSI-high is broadly supported, but the low mutation-burden context remains non-evaluable because no MSI-high cases satisfy that stratum. The most informative next analysis is the narrowed active set: H233-H235 test SMARCA4, KEAP1, and TP53 in backgrounds lacking TP53, SMARCA4, KEAP1, PTEN, and MSI-high; H248 tests MSI-high after removing those four losses; H240, H244, and H245 test PTEN in triple-intact MSI-negative cells across central mutation burden and aneuploidy extremes. These tests address whether the large associations are independent of each other and whether the smaller PTEN association is stable in cleaner central strata. All conclusions remain observational associations in the supplied 2000-cell lung-cell-line dataset and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, clinical utility, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated after iteration 16 synthesize. All estimates are signed to registered direction; direction -1 positive means stronger dependency, direction +1 positive means weaker dependency. Threshold 0.15 composite dependency units. Validation budget exhausted. Robust accepted within-dataset associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger (R4/R13; MSI-negative R195; middle TMB R198), KEAP1 loss weaker (R6/R26; MSI-negative R196; middle TMB R199), TP53 loss weaker (R1/R39; MSI-negative R197; middle TMB R200), MSI-high stronger (R88/R93; middle TMB R189). PTEN loss accepted overall and in selected cleaner contexts (R9/R66; R132; R44/R53; R205; R203), but many context estimates are borderline. Downgraded H127 and H134 to unresolved/closed due lower bounds below threshold/null (R117/R120 and R122/R133). No supported interaction. Negative/unsupported: other drivers, markers, technical/culture/library/batch/omics/sex. Direct continuous signature tests invalid due insufficient cells (R170/R171/R172), not evidence of null. Active high-priority next tests: H233-H235 four-loss-clean MSI-negative main effects; H248 MSI-high in four-loss clean background; H240 PTEN four-loss clean middle mutation burden; H244/H245 PTEN four-loss clean low/high aneuploidy. Closed lower-priority active claims: H236-H239 middle Cas9, H241-H243 PTEN middle Cas9/aneuploidy/screen ROC, H246-H247 PTEN growth extremes. All observational within supplied dataset only."
